{"comment_text": {"ja466:0.1": "", "ja466:0.2": "", "ja466:0.3": "", "ja466:0.4": "", "ja466:1.1": "A castaway reflects on the abundance of his lonely isle. ", "ja466:1.2": "", "ja466:1.3": "", "ja466:1.4": "", "ja466:2.1": "A righteous god stands in the north and warns the newly arrived refugees. ", "ja466:2.2": "", "ja466:2.3": "", "ja466:2.4": "", "ja466:3.1": "A wicked god speaks in the south. ", "ja466:3.2": "", "ja466:3.3": "", "ja466:3.4": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Modathavho</i> is second imperative plural reflexive, “Let you all celebrate”. ", "ja466:4.1": "", "ja466:4.2": "", "ja466:4.3": "", "ja466:4.4": "Here <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ā</i> is a separate preposition, glossed by <i lang='pi' translate='no'>yāva</i>. ", "ja466:5.1": "A foolish refugee endorses the southern god. ", "ja466:5.2": "", "ja466:5.3": "", "ja466:5.4": "", "ja466:6.1": "A wise refugee counsels action. ", "ja466:6.2": "", "ja466:6.3": "", "ja466:6.4": "", "ja466:7.1": "", "ja466:7.2": "", "ja466:7.3": "", "ja466:7.4": "", "ja466:7.5": "", "ja466:7.6": "", "ja466:8.1": "", "ja466:8.2": "", "ja466:8.3": "", "ja466:8.4": "", "ja466:9.1": "", "ja466:9.2": "", "ja466:9.3": "", "ja466:9.4": "", "ja466:10.1": "These editorializing verses are attributed to the Buddha. ", "ja466:10.2": "", "ja466:10.3": "", "ja466:10.4": "", "ja466:11.1": "", "ja466:11.2": "", "ja466:11.3": "", "ja466:11.4": "", "ja466:12.1": "", "ja466:12.2": "", "ja466:12.3": "", "ja466:12.4": "", "ja466:13.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja466:0.1": "<article id='ja466'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja466:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja466:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja466:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja466:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:2.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:2.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:2.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:2.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:3.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:3.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:3.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:3.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:4.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:4.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:4.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:4.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:5.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:5.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:5.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:5.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:6.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:6.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:6.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:6.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:7.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:7.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:7.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:7.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:7.5": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:7.6": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:8.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:8.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:8.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:8.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:9.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:9.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:9.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:9.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:10.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:10.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:10.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:10.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:11.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:11.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:11.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:11.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p>", "ja466:12.1": "<p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:12.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:12.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja466:12.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja466:13.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja466:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja466:0.2": "Dvādasakanipāta ", "ja466:0.3": "Cūḷakuṇālavagga ", "ja466:0.4": "3. Samuddavāṇijajātaka ", "ja466:1.1": "“Kasanti vapanti te janā, ", "ja466:1.2": "Manujā kammaphalūpajīvino; ", "ja466:1.3": "Nayimassa dīpakassa bhāgino, ", "ja466:1.4": "Jambudīpā idameva no varaṁ”. ", "ja466:2.1": "“Tipañcarattūpagatamhi cande, ", "ja466:2.2": "Vego mahā hehiti sāgarassa; ", "ja466:2.3": "Uplavissaṁ dīpamimaṁ uḷāraṁ, ", "ja466:2.4": "Mā vo vadhī gacchatha leṇamaññaṁ”. ", "ja466:3.1": "“Na jātuyaṁ sāgaravārivego, ", "ja466:3.2": "Uplavissaṁ dīpamimaṁ uḷāraṁ; ", "ja466:3.3": "Taṁ me nimittehi bahūhi diṭṭhaṁ, ", "ja466:3.4": "Mā bhetha kiṁ socatha modathavho. ", "ja466:4.1": "Pahūtabhakkhaṁ bahuannapānaṁ, ", "ja466:4.2": "Pattattha āvāsamimaṁ uḷāraṁ; ", "ja466:4.3": "Na vo bhayaṁ paṭipassāmi kiñci, ", "ja466:4.4": "Āputtaputtehi pamodathavho”. ", "ja466:5.1": "“Yo devoyaṁ dakkhiṇāyaṁ disāyaṁ, ", "ja466:5.2": "Khemanti pakkosati tassa saccaṁ; ", "ja466:5.3": "Na uttaro vedi bhayābhayassa, ", "ja466:5.4": "Mā bhetha kiṁ socatha modathavho”. ", "ja466:6.1": "“Yathā ime vippavadanti yakkhā, ", "ja466:6.2": "Eko bhayaṁ saṁsati khemameko; ", "ja466:6.3": "Tadiṅgha mayhaṁ vacanaṁ suṇātha, ", "ja466:6.4": "Khippaṁ lahuṁ mā vinassimha sabbe. ", "ja466:7.1": "Sabbe samāgamma karoma nāvaṁ, ", "ja466:7.2": "Doṇiṁ daḷhaṁ sabbayantūpapannaṁ; ", "ja466:7.3": "Sace ayaṁ dakkhiṇo saccamāha, ", "ja466:7.4": "Moghaṁ paṭikkosati uttaroyaṁ; ", "ja466:7.5": "Sā ceva no hehiti āpadatthā, ", "ja466:7.6": "Imañca dīpaṁ na pariccajema. ", "ja466:8.1": "Sace ca kho uttaro saccamāha, ", "ja466:8.2": "Moghaṁ paṭikkosati dakkhiṇoyaṁ; ", "ja466:8.3": "Tameva nāvaṁ abhiruyha sabbe, ", "ja466:8.4": "Evaṁ mayaṁ sotthi taremu pāraṁ. ", "ja466:9.1": "Na ve sugaṇhaṁ paṭhamena seṭṭhaṁ, ", "ja466:9.2": "Kaniṭṭhamāpāthagataṁ gahetvā; ", "ja466:9.3": "Yo cīdha tacchaṁ paviceyya gaṇhati, ", "ja466:9.4": "Sa ve naro seṭṭhamupeti ṭhānaṁ. ", "ja466:10.1": "Yathāpi te sāgaravārimajjhe, ", "ja466:10.2": "Sakammunā sotthi vahiṁsu vāṇijā; ", "ja466:10.3": "Anāgatatthaṁ paṭivijjhiyāna, ", "ja466:10.4": "Appampi nācceti sa bhūripañño. ", "ja466:11.1": "Bālā ca mohena rasānugiddhā, ", "ja466:11.2": "Anāgataṁ appaṭivijjhiyatthaṁ; ", "ja466:11.3": "Paccuppanne sīdanti atthajāte, ", "ja466:11.4": "Samuddamajjhe yathā te manussā. ", "ja466:12.1": "Anāgataṁ paṭikayirātha kiccaṁ, ", "ja466:12.2": "‘Mā maṁ kiccaṁ kiccakāle byadhesi’; ", "ja466:12.3": "Taṁ tādisaṁ paṭikatakiccakāriṁ, ", "ja466:12.4": "Na taṁ kiccaṁ kiccakāle byadhetī”ti. ", "ja466:13.1": "Samuddavāṇijajātakaṁ tatiyaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja466:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 466 ", "ja466:0.2": "The Book of the Twelves ", "ja466:0.3": "The Chapter With Cūḷakuṇāla ", "ja466:0.4": "The Sea Merchants: a past life story ", "ja466:1.1": "“Those folk sow and reap, ", "ja466:1.2": "men living on the fruit of their work. ", "ja466:1.3": "They have no share of this island. ", "ja466:1.4": "This is better far than India!” ", "ja466:2.1": "“When the fifteenth day full moon has risen, ", "ja466:2.2": "there will be a great flood from the sea, ", "ja466:2.3": "drowning this splendid isle. ", "ja466:2.4": "Let it not destroy you all! Go to some other haven!” ", "ja466:3.1": "“Never shall a mighty flood of water from the sea ", "ja466:3.2": "drown this splendid isle—", "ja466:3.3": "I have seen that through many a sign. ", "ja466:3.4": "Don’t fear! Why worry? Celebrate! ", "ja466:4.1": "You’ve come to this splendid abode, ", "ja466:4.2": "full of food and drink. ", "ja466:4.3": "I see no danger for you at all. ", "ja466:4.4": "Celebrate, even unto the sons of sons!” ", "ja466:5.1": "“This god in the southern quarter ", "ja466:5.2": "crying, ‘It is safe!’: his is the truth! ", "ja466:5.3": "The northern doesn’t know if there’s a danger or not. ", "ja466:5.4": "Don’t fear! Why worry? Celebrate!” ", "ja466:6.1": "“As these spirits argue, ", "ja466:6.2": "one reporting danger, one safety, ", "ja466:6.3": "please heed my advice, ", "ja466:6.4": "lest we perish swift and fleet. ", "ja466:7.1": "Let all join together to build a boat, ", "ja466:7.2": "a strong vessel fully equipped. ", "ja466:7.3": "If this southern one speaks true, ", "ja466:7.4": "and is falsely rejected by the northern, ", "ja466:7.5": "it shall serve us in time of need, ", "ja466:7.6": "and we would not give up the island. ", "ja466:8.1": "But if the northern speaks true, ", "ja466:8.2": "and is falsely rejected by the southern, ", "ja466:8.3": "then having all boarded the boat, ", "ja466:8.4": "we shall cross safely to the far shore. ", "ja466:9.1": "Truly, best not accept the last word that came your way, ", "ja466:9.2": "when what was spoken by the first was best. ", "ja466:9.3": "Who here accepts the truth after examination, ", "ja466:9.4": "that man goes to the best place.” ", "ja466:10.1": "Just as, in the middle of the watery sea, ", "ja466:10.2": "the merchants fled to safety by their own efforts, ", "ja466:10.3": "so, realizing his future welfare, ", "ja466:10.4": "he of vast wisdom transgresses not at all. ", "ja466:11.1": "Fools deluded by desire for tastes, ", "ja466:11.2": "not realizing their future welfare, ", "ja466:11.3": "sink down in face of present need, ", "ja466:11.4": "like those people in mid-ocean. ", "ja466:12.1": "Prepare what must be done for the future, thinking, ", "ja466:12.2": "“Let what must be done not harm me on the day the duty ripens.” ", "ja466:12.3": "The kind who acts to prepare what must be done, ", "ja466:12.4": "is not harmed by what must be done on the day the duty ripens. ", "ja466:13.1": ""}, "variant_text": {"ja466:0.1": "", "ja466:0.2": "", "ja466:0.3": "", "ja466:0.4": "", "ja466:1.1": "", "ja466:1.2": "", "ja466:1.3": "", "ja466:1.4": "", "ja466:2.1": "", "ja466:2.2": "", "ja466:2.3": "", "ja466:2.4": "", "ja466:3.1": "", "ja466:3.2": "", "ja466:3.3": "", "ja466:3.4": "modathavho → modatha vo (mr) ", "ja466:4.1": "", "ja466:4.2": "", "ja466:4.3": "", "ja466:4.4": "", "ja466:5.1": "dakkhiṇāyaṁ → dakkhiṇassaṁ (bj) ", "ja466:5.2": "", "ja466:5.3": "", "ja466:5.4": "", "ja466:6.1": "", "ja466:6.2": "", "ja466:6.3": "", "ja466:6.4": "", "ja466:7.1": "", "ja466:7.2": "", "ja466:7.3": "", "ja466:7.4": "", "ja466:7.5": "", "ja466:7.6": "", "ja466:8.1": "", "ja466:8.2": "", "ja466:8.3": "", "ja466:8.4": "", "ja466:9.1": "", "ja466:9.2": "", "ja466:9.3": "tacchaṁ → majjhaṁ (bj, sya1ed, sya2ed, pts-vp-pli1) | gaṇhati → gaṇhi (mr) ", "ja466:9.4": "", "ja466:10.1": "", "ja466:10.2": "", "ja466:10.3": "", "ja466:10.4": "", "ja466:11.1": "", "ja466:11.2": "", "ja466:11.3": "", "ja466:11.4": "", "ja466:12.1": "", "ja466:12.2": "", "ja466:12.3": "paṭikatakiccakāriṁ → paṭigata … (bj); paṭikataṁ … (mr); paṭikacca … (?) ", "ja466:12.4": "", "ja466:13.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja466:0.1": "", "ja466:0.2": "", "ja466:0.3": "", "ja466:0.4": "", "ja466:1.1": "csp1ed22.244, csp2ed22.244, ms22J_2265, msdiv25, ndp22.236, pts-vp-pli4.160", "ja466:1.2": "", "ja466:1.3": "", "ja466:1.4": "", "ja466:2.1": "dr27.324, ms22J_2266, msdiv26, pts-vp-pli4.162, sya27.326", "ja466:2.2": "", "ja466:2.3": "", "ja466:2.4": "", "ja466:3.1": "ms22J_2267, msdiv27", "ja466:3.2": "", "ja466:3.3": "", "ja466:3.4": "", "ja466:4.1": "bj30.418, ms22J_2268, msdiv28", "ja466:4.2": "", "ja466:4.3": "", "ja466:4.4": "", "ja466:5.1": "ms22J_2269, msdiv29, pts-vp-pli4.163", "ja466:5.2": "", "ja466:5.3": "", "ja466:5.4": "", "ja466:6.1": "ms22J_2270, msdiv30, sya27.327", "ja466:6.2": "", "ja466:6.3": "", "ja466:6.4": "", "ja466:7.1": "csp1ed22.245, csp2ed22.245, dr27.325, ms22J_2271, msdiv31, ndp22.237", "ja466:7.2": "", "ja466:7.3": "", "ja466:7.4": "", "ja466:7.5": "", "ja466:7.6": "", "ja466:8.1": "ms22J_2272, msdiv32, pts-vp-pli4.164", "ja466:8.2": "", "ja466:8.3": "", "ja466:8.4": "", "ja466:9.1": "ms22J_2273, msdiv33", "ja466:9.2": "", "ja466:9.3": "", "ja466:9.4": "", "ja466:10.1": "ms22J_2274, msdiv34, pts-vp-pli4.165", "ja466:10.2": "", "ja466:10.3": "", "ja466:10.4": "", "ja466:11.1": "bj30.420, ms22J_2275, msdiv35, sya27.328", "ja466:11.2": "", "ja466:11.3": "", "ja466:11.4": "", "ja466:12.1": "dr27.326, ms22J_2276, msdiv36, ndp22.238, pts-vp-pli4.166, vri68.191", "ja466:12.2": "", "ja466:12.3": "", "ja466:12.4": "", "ja466:13.1": "ms22J_2277"}, "keys_order": ["ja466:0.1", "ja466:0.2", "ja466:0.3", "ja466:0.4", "ja466:1.1", "ja466:1.2", "ja466:1.3", "ja466:1.4", "ja466:2.1", "ja466:2.2", "ja466:2.3", "ja466:2.4", "ja466:3.1", "ja466:3.2", "ja466:3.3", "ja466:3.4", "ja466:4.1", "ja466:4.2", "ja466:4.3", "ja466:4.4", "ja466:5.1", "ja466:5.2", "ja466:5.3", "ja466:5.4", "ja466:6.1", "ja466:6.2", "ja466:6.3", "ja466:6.4", "ja466:7.1", "ja466:7.2", "ja466:7.3", "ja466:7.4", "ja466:7.5", "ja466:7.6", "ja466:8.1", "ja466:8.2", "ja466:8.3", "ja466:8.4", "ja466:9.1", "ja466:9.2", "ja466:9.3", "ja466:9.4", "ja466:10.1", "ja466:10.2", "ja466:10.3", "ja466:10.4", "ja466:11.1", "ja466:11.2", "ja466:11.3", "ja466:11.4", "ja466:12.1", "ja466:12.2", "ja466:12.3", "ja466:12.4", "ja466:13.1"]}